    lead:"Chile is an authoritarian military-national balancer under <a href='augusto-pinochet.html'>Augusto Pinochet</a>. Its <a href='santiago-doctrine.html'>Doctrine of National Equilibrium</a> combines American and British security relationships, selected Japanese and Latin development, diversified procurement, strategic copper ownership, and explicit refusal of permanent foreign bases.",
    canon:"<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-w3z2k writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:15:00-06:00 -->Pinochet's authoritarian balancing regime, severe repression, non-Chicago economic direction, Santiago Doctrine, spring-1984 Plan Centinela with 25,000–35,000 personnel, and the strategic-level 1986–89 Cold Andes are established.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup> The road to power, officers' crisis, elected predecessor, coup, junta, copper regime, intelligence service, constitutional order, detailed economy, British arrangements, Beagle chronology, later transition, and any 1989–92 war remain working or open.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->",
