replaceChileSection("chile","position","<p>Chile is not equidistant: Washington is the power it is least able to defy, while Britain is its preferred professional military partner. Japanese and Latin relationships supply development and institutional alternatives without receiving a base, strategic monopoly, or political veto.</p>");
replaceChileSection("chile","economy","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-w4a3m writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:15:00-06:00 --><p>The regime is not historical Chicago-school neoliberalism and borrows selectively from Japan and the Latin bloc; mature Chile balances through local firms and strong but nonexclusive American commerce.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup> State copper control, development banks, procurement policy, education, private-sector boundaries, and investment rules remain working implementation.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
replaceChileSection("chile","security","<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-w5b4n writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:15:00-06:00 --><p>The armed forces sustain Pinochet's regime and the established American–British security lean.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup> Procurement division by function, deliberate interoperability costs, a centralized intelligence service, and the exact foreign surveillance arrangements remain working institutional detail.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->");
appendChileSection("chile",{id:"road-to-military-rule",title:"Road to military rule",html:"<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-w6c5p writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:15:00-06:00 --><p>The 1966–68 Officers' Crisis, Popular National Front, early-1970s copper breakdown, military coup, four-service junta, and Pinochet's late compromise emergence constitute a working route to his established authoritarian rule rather than fixed domestic chronology.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->"});
appendChileSection("chile",{id:"southern-confrontation",title:"Southern confrontation",html:"<!-- altwwii-writer-block:start id=wb-g-20260815-w7d6q writer=g kind=revision created=2026-08-15T23:15:00-06:00 --><p><a href='plan-centinela.html'>Plan Centinela</a> withheld Argentine reserves from the Falklands and helped produce the strategic-level <a href='cold-andes.html'>Cold Andes</a>.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='a'>[a]</sup> The Beagle crisis as the specific legal precursor and the detailed postwar arms competition remain working continuity.<sup class='canon-note' data-provenance='e'>[e]</sup></p><!-- altwwii-writer-block:end -->"});
